    {
      "id": "claim_42879d040408456eab6c80926944423d",
      "statement": "Migrations are a map[int]string of schema version to DDL applied in ascending order in migrate.go: a meta key/value table is created in Open before migrations run and stores schema_version, currentSchemaVersion reads meta (0 when absent), and each unapplied version runs in its own transaction (DDL then INSERT OR REPLACE schema_version then commit, rolling back on failure); DB.SchemaVersion returns the applied version.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/storage/migrate.go#L10-L119",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3edf8f4df184715ca29c389687de5502da553fad9b6daf25b4dd2697a19a192e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bfe6f685ff8b4c2eb8ecca9a6d8e25dc",
      "statement": "The base schema (version 1) creates four tables with ON DELETE CASCADE FKs down session -> message -> part: session (id PK, project_dir, title, model, agent, cost, time_created, time_updated; cost kept for parity but ignored by SessionFromRow), message (id PK, session_id FK, role, agent, cost REAL, tokens TEXT JSON, time_created, time_completed), part (id PK, message_id FK, session_id, type, tool, state_json, time_created), and permission (request_id PK, session_id, action, resource, response, always_json, time_created); version 2 adds the todo table (session_id FK cascade, content, status, priority, position) and an index on session_id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/storage/migrate.go#L16-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48b46162505cd7a20a88e09e4e6b6415bff05334776ccc8fe5a841b479cbb865:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9145094ede4d4dd6b0dfd053bdec5d0e",
      "statement": "All DAOs use parameterized queries only (? placeholders), following the golang-database policy; sessions DAO provides CreateSession (empty agent defaults to build via agentOrDefault), GetSession (missing id -> ErrNotFound), ListSessions (newest time_updated first, optional LIMIT), UpdateSession (zero-valued patch fields untouched, no-op patch returns nil, RowsAffected 0 -> ErrNotFound), and DeleteSession (messages/parts cascade).",
      "evidence": [
